<title>PARAGUAY: SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT COLOMBIA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT COLOMBIA 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay beat Colombia 2-1</p>
<p>(halftime 1-0) in a South American World Cup qualifier on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers</p>
<p>Paraguay - Carlos Gamarra (6th minute), Derlis Soto (88th)</p>
<p>Colombia - Maurico Serna (87th, penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Paraguay     9  6  2  1  12  5 20</p>
<p> Colombia     9  5  2  2  15  8 17</p>
<p> Bolivia	9  3  4  2  14  9 13</p>
<p> Ecuador	9  4  1  4  13 10 13</p>
<p> Argentina    9  3  4  2  12  9 13</p>
<p> Uruguay	9  4  1  4   9 11 13</p>
<p> Peru	   9  2  4  3  10 12 10</p>
<p> Chile	  8  2  3  3  11 12  9</p>
<p> Venezuela    9  0  1  8   6 26  1</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
